# Go 1.26+ recommended style (mandatory)

On **every** Go edit in this repo, use the recommended modern form when it is a drop-in. Do not leave older patterns in new or touched code.

## Required preferences

| Prefer | Instead of |
|--------|------------|
| `min` / `max` | if-clamp (`if x < 0 { x = 0 }`) |
| `new(expr)` | `intPtr` / `mustInt` / `&v` helpers |
| `errors.AsType[T](err)` | `var x T; errors.As(err, &x)` |
| `maps.Copy` | hand-rolled map copy loops |
| `strings.Cut` / `CutPrefix` / `CutSuffix` | `Index`+slice or `HasPrefix`+`TrimPrefix` when you need the rest |
| `strings.SplitSeq` / `FieldsSeq` | `Split`/`Fields` only to range and discard the slice |
| `for i := range n` | `for i := 0; i < n; i++` when `i` is not mutated |
| `slices.Sort*` / `cmp.*` | `sort.Slice` / hand-rolled multi-key compares |
| `encoding/hex` | `fmt.Sprintf("%x", …)` for digests |
| `math/rand/v2` | `math/rand` in new tests |

## Required finish checklist

1. Run `go fix -diff ./...` (or `go fix ./...`) and apply safe modernizer fixes.
2. Delete helpers made unused by the rewrite (no leftover `//go:fix inline` stubs).
3. Re-run tests for touched packages.
4. Confirm `go fix -diff` is clean for packages you changed.

## Do not over-apply

- Keep `for i := 0; …; i++` when the body mutates `i` (option parsers skipping args).
- Do not swap `omitempty` → `omitzero` without reviewing the JSON wire contract.
- Stay within the `go` version in `go.mod`.

Full policy: `AGENTS.md` and `CONTRIBUTING.md` (Go style).
